    "notes": [
      "H1 (execute a host binary): HOST_ESCAPE_CURRENTLY_BLOCKED_BY_ENVIRONMENT. measured OUTSIDE the sandbox in Ubuntu: EXIT=126 The refusal is a property of the environment, so it is recorded as environmental and is NOT counted as sandbox evidence — while the probe is still required to have been permitted and to have reached the boundary.",
      "Probes R7, R8, R9, W2, W6 reported exit 0 while the host filesystem was unaffected: the sandbox presents a denied region as an empty ephemeral overlay rather than refusing the syscall. Containment holds, but a Producer running there would BELIEVE its write succeeded, so its self-reports about files outside the worktree are worth nothing."
